+</style><style>main#main .detail-hero .detail-sub{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is a small city on the Waccamaw River, said WAH-kuh-maw. Much of downtown was built in the early 1900s, after a fire, and its streets have old live oaks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Riverwalk, a boardwalk along the river, is about 3 minutes by car from the center of town.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing under tall sycamores, beside old wooden buildings on the river in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town is older than the beach towns. It was laid out in 1732, as Kingston, and later named Conwayborough for General Robert Conway of the state militia. The name became Conway in 1883.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">City Hall on Main Street was built in 1824 and 1825 as the county courthouse. Its design is credited to Robert Mills, who designed the Washington Monument.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-hall-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="800" alt="Conway City Hall, a brick building with a white portico of four columns and stairs up both sides, beside a white clock tower and palmetto trees" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia</a></span></div><figcaption>Conway City Hall on Main Street, built in 1824 and 1825 as the county courthouse.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Coastal Carolina University is inside the city, about 10 minutes from downtown. It enrolled 11,348 students in fall 2024, a record for the school.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city is growing fast. It grew about 22 percent from 2020 to 2025, by Census estimates, the seventh fastest among South Carolina cities and towns of 10,000 or more. About 30,600 people lived there in 2025.</p><figure class="c3-cw-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-downtown-conway" viewBox="0 0 360 380" width="360" height="380" role="img" aria-label="Map of Conway and the coast: from downtown Conway, the beach in Myrtle Beach is about 25 minutes by car, the airport about 25 minutes, and Coastal Carolina University and Conway Medical Center about 10 minutes each." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-downtown-conway text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#