" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-airport" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="-15" y="-11.2" text-anchor="end"><tspan x="-15">Myrtle Beach</tspan><tspan x="-15" dy="16.5">airport</tspan></text><text class="m" x="-15" y="20.8" text-anchor="end">about 25 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(85 130.2)"><g class="k"><rect x="9.9" y="-38.6" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="9.9" y="-39.9" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-town" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="11.9" y="-24.9"><tspan x="11.9">University</tspan></text><text class="m" x="11.9" y="-9.4">about 10 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(113.4 145.9)"><g class="k"><rect x="13" y="-16.7" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="13" y="-18" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-hospital" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="15" y="-3"><tspan x="15">Hospital</tspan></text><text class="m" x="15" y="12.5">about 10 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(45 65.2)"><g class="k"><g transform="scale(0.8)"><ellipse cx="0" cy="1" rx="7" ry="2.4" fill="#1c2028" opacity=".18"/><path d="M0 0C-3-6-13-14-13-26a13 13 0 1 1 26 0c0 12-10 20-13 26z" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-home" x="-8.5" y="-34.5" width="17" height="17" color="#ffffff"/></g><text class="h" x="15" y="-14.5"><tspan x="15">Downtown Conway</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg></div><figcaption>Drive times by car from downtown Conway, without traffic. In our experience, rush hour adds 5 to 10 minutes. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">Is a Conway address inside the city of Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not. Of about 30,300 homes with a Conway mailing address, only about 8,300, a little more than 1 in 4, are inside the city limits. The rest are in unincorporated Horry County.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes with a Conway mailing address"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes with a Conway mailing address</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where the home is</span><span role="columnheader">Homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inside the city limits</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.379" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 8,300</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Outside, in the county</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 22,000</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The same is true of homes for sale. At our last count, 172 of the 673 houses for sale with a Conway address were inside the city.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city line changes your tax bill: about $670 a year more inside it on a typical house you live in (the yearly cost is below). We tell you which side of the line a house is on before you make an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="parts-of-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Five parts of town">Which part of Conway should you look at?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city's homes fall into five parts, each with something the others do not have. Pick by what you want most:</p><style>main#main .c3-gcards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(15rem,1fr));gap:.7rem;max-width:760px;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}main#main .c3-gcard{padding:.75rem .9rem .8rem;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.75);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(28,32,40,.08);backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%)}main#main .c3-gcard h3{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 .35rem!important;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem!important;font-weight:650;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gcard h3 .i{display:inline-flex;color:var(--brass)}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gi{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0}main#main .c3-gcard a{color:var(--navy)}@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:reduce){main#main .c3-gcard{backdrop-filter:none;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none;background:#fbf8f3}}</style><div class="c3-gcards"><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span>Walk to Main Street and the river</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#downtown">1. Downtown</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span>No home in a flood map</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#us-501">2. Near the university</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span>The lowest prices</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#west-and-south">3. West and south</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 16v-4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h10.5l2 5M14.5 11l4-7H21M8.5 17.5h4M2 21.5h20"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/></svg></span>The biggest lots</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#north-edge">5. The north edge</a></li></ul></div></div><figure class="c3-cw-fig"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-flood-map.svg" width="760" height="830" alt="Map of the city of Conway with its five parts numbered: 1 downtown, 2 near the university, off US 501, 3 west and south, 4 around Crabtree Swamp, 5 the north edge. Light blue is FEMA's high-risk flood zone; dark blue is where Florence's water reached in 2018. Both are mostly along the Waccamaw River and the swamps north of downtown." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ul class="c3-cw-legend" aria-label="Map colors"><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#8fb3c7"></span>FEMA's high-risk flood zone</li><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Where Florence's water reached</li><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#fffdf9;border:2px solid #1c2028"></span>City limits</li></ul>About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both blue areas. The orange square is Coastal Carolina University. Map data: Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.</figcaption><ol class="c3-cw-key" aria-label="The five parts of Conway"><li><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><a href="#downtown">Downtown</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><a href="#us-501">Near the university, off US 501</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><a href="#west-and-south">West and south</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><a href="#crabtree-swamp">Around Crabtree Swamp</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span><a href="#north-edge">The north edge</a></li></ol></figure><h3 id="downtown" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Downtown: a walk to Main Street and the river</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown here means the streets within about a mile of the center of town, with about 1,160 homes. A typical house lot is about a third of an acre.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The largest subdivisions are Snowhill, Mayfair, Buckwood, Highland Park and Collinswood. Main Street, City Hall and the Riverwalk are all in this part of town.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An older white wood house with black shutters behind a large live oak, with a paved driveway, in downtown Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>An older house under a live oak, a few blocks from Main Street.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few homes here come up for sale: 22 resold in the past year, for about $275,000 in the middle, with a wide spread. 36 homes, about 3 in 100, are in a flood map.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Downtown%20Conway">Book a showing in Downtown Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="us-501" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>Near the university, off US 501: no home in a flood map</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Along US 501 toward the beach, the city reaches past Coastal Carolina University. Wild Wing, Coastal Point West, Kiskadee Parke and Aviary Village are the largest subdivisions, with about 1,430 homes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By the county's map, Florence's water did not reach this part of Conway. None of its homes are in either flood map.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A red brick library building with white doors behind a wide live oak with long low limbs, at Coastal Carolina University in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: LittleT889. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: LittleT889</a></span></div><figcaption>Kimbel Library at Coastal Carolina University, under a live oak.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lots are about four-tenths of an acre. Homes here resold for about $365,000 in the past year, with a wide spread. Only homes at the north edge resold for more.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Conway%20near%20the%20university">Book a showing in Conway near the university<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-and-south" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>West and south: the most homes and the lowest prices</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West and south of downtown, toward US 378 and US 701 South, is the largest part of the city, with about 3,400 homes. Rosehaven, New Castle, Oak Glenn, Woodland Lakes and Jasmine Woods are the largest subdivisions.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes here resold for about $245,000 in the past year, the lowest middle price of the five parts. Lots are about a quarter of an acre.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rosehaven, Oak Glenn and Woodland Lakes have no homes in either flood map. 176 homes in this part, about 5 in 100, are in one; the largest groups are in Kingston Village, Pecan Grove and Sedgefield.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=West%20Conway">Book a showing in West Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="crabtree-swamp" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>Around Crabtree Swamp: close to downtown, but check the street</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North and northwest of downtown, around Crabtree Swamp, are about 2,390 homes in Midtown Village, Rivertown Row, Elmhurst, Woodcreek, Kingston Bay, Sherwood and Country Club Forest.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This is the part of Conway where flooding is most common: 253 homes, about 1 in 10, are in a flood map. Most of them are in a few subdivisions near the swamp, Sherwood above all. Rivertown Row and Kingston Bay have none.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes here resold for about $260,000 in the past year, on the smallest lots in the city, about a fifth of an acre.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Conway">Book a showing in North Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="north-edge" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span>The north edge: the biggest lots in the city</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the city's north edge, 4 to 5 miles from downtown, are about 560 homes in Ridgewood West, Country Manor, Maple Hill and smaller subdivisions. A typical lot here is about three-quarters of an acre, the largest in the city.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Florence's water did not reach these streets on the county's map. 15 homes are in FEMA's high-risk zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only 25 homes resold here in the past year, for about $400,000 in the middle.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Conway%2C%20larger%20lots">Book a showing in North Conway, larger lots<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:49.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The five parts of Conway side by side</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part of town</th><th scope="col">Homes</th><th scope="col">Typical lot</th><th scope="col">Homes resold for</th><th scope="col">Homes in a flood map</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">1. Downtown</th><td data-label="Homes">About 1,200</td><td data-label="Typical lot">About a third of an acre</td><td data-label="Homes resold for">About $275,000</td><td data-label="Homes in a flood map">36 (3 in 100)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2. Near the university, off US 501</th><td data-label="Homes">About 1,400</td><td data-label="Typical lot">About four-tenths of an acre</td><td data-label="Homes resold for">About $365,000</td><td data-label="Homes in a flood map">None</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3. West and south</th><td data-label="Homes">About 3,400</td><td data-label="Typical lot">About a quarter of an acre</td><td data-label="Homes resold for">About $245,000</td><td data-label="Homes in a flood map">176 (5 in 100)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4. Around Crabtree Swamp</th><td data-label="Homes">About 2,400</td><td data-label="Typical lot">About a fifth of an acre</td><td data-label="Homes resold for">About $260,000</td><td data-label="Homes in a flood map">253 (11 in 100)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5. The north edge</th><td data-label="Homes">About 560</td><td data-label="Typical lot">About three-quarters of an acre</td><td data-label="Homes resold for">About $400,000</td><td data-label="Homes in a flood map">15 (3 in 100)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Conway, SC flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some parts do, and badly. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both flood maps. The other 480 or so are near the river, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The worst flood on record came after Hurricane Florence in 2018. The river at Conway crested at 21.16 feet. Major flooding starts at 14 feet.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why the flood comes late and stays</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The flood here comes down the river, days after the storm. Florence came ashore in North Carolina, and the river at Conway crested 12 days later.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-cw-fig" style="max-width:640px"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">How high the river at Conway rose, in feet, after two hurricanes</span><ul class="c3-cw-legend"><li><span class="c3-cw-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Florence, 2018</li><li><span class="c3-cw-line" style="background:#5c6b78"></span>Matthew, 2016</li></ul><svg class="c3-cw-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the Waccamaw River's height at Conway, by days after the storm came ashore. After Florence the river rose past flood stage (11 feet) on day 2, crested at about 21 feet on day 12, and stayed above flood stage for 29 days. After Matthew it crested at about 18 feet on day 10 and stayed above flood stage for 26 days."><rect x="34" y="12" width="318" height="202" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.55)" rx="6"/><rect x="34" y="12" width="318" height="101" fill="#2f6f8f" fill-opacity=".07"/><line x1="34" y1="150.9" x2="352" y2="150.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/><text class="ct" x="352" y="145.9" text-anchor="end">Flood stage, 11 ft</text><line x1="34" y1="113" x2="352" y2="113" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><text class="ct" x="352" y="108" text-anchor="end">Major flooding, 14 ft</text><line x1="76" y1="12" x2="76" y2="214" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35" stroke-width="1"/><path d="M34 178.1L40 178.3L46 178.6L52 178.6L58 178.1L64 178.1L70 176.6L76 147.6L82 105.6L88 100.9L94 103.4L100 100.8L106 92.2L112 83.1L118 75.1L124 68.9L130 65.4L136 64.5L142 66.3L148 70.2L154 75.9L160 82.8L166 91L172 99.1L178 106.6L184 113.9L190 120.8L196 126.6L202 131.7L208 136.5L214 141L220 145.7L226 149.9L232 154.2L238 159L244 163.6L250 167.4L256 171.7L262 175.2L268 177.4L274 180L280 181.2L286 182.1L292 181.3L298 180.3L304 181.7L310 183.3L316 185.1L322 186.9L328 187.7L334 193.3L340 193.4L346 193.9L352 196.1" fill="none" stroke="#5c6b78" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M40 194.3L46 192.2L52 189.9L58 189L64 188L70 188.1L76 193.5L82 172.7L88 143.2L94 104.9L100 94.8L106 99.7L112 93.1L118 71.7L124 50L130 35.4L136 27.3L142 23.5L148 23L154 25.1L160 29.5L166 35.5L172 42.3L178 51.6L184 61.9L190 72.9L196 84.3L202 95.8L208 105.7L214 114.8L220 122.3L226 128.1L232 132.3L238 135.9L244 139.6L250 144.4L256 149.1L262 153.1L268 157.1L274 160.3L280 164.8L286 168.4L292 170.2L298 171.6L304 171.2L310 168.6L316 167.3L322 167.5L328 167.7L334 167.7L340 172.1L346 177.8L352 181.6" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="148" cy="23" r="4" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5"/><text class="cl" x="156" y="28" fill="#91592b">Crest, day 12</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="193.3" text-anchor="end">8</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="155.4" text-anchor="end">11</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="117.5" text-anchor="end">14</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="79.6" text-anchor="end">17</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="41.8" text-anchor="end">20</text><line x1="76" y1="214" x2="76" y2="219" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="76" y="236" text-anchor="middle">0</text><line x1="136" y1="214" x2="136" y2="219" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="136" y="236" text-anchor="middle">10</text><line x1="196" y1="214" x2="196" y2="219" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="196" y="236" text-anchor="middle">20</text><line x1="256" y1="214" x2="256" y2="219" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="256" y="236" text-anchor="middle">30</text><line x1="316" y1="214" x2="316" y2="219" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="316" y="236" text-anchor="middle">40</text><text class="ct" x="193" y="248" text-anchor="middle">Days after the storm came ashore</text></svg><figcaption>Daily average height on the river gauge at the Conway Marina. After Florence, the river stayed above flood stage for 29 days, 20 of them in major flood.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">During Florence, the county closed 58 streets in and at the edge of the city for flooding. Long Avenue, Third Avenue, Church Street and Marina Drive stayed closed about four weeks.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which streets flood at each river height</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The National Weather Service lists what floods as the river rises:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">River height</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What floods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Low areas along Long Avenue and Sherwood Drive, near Crabtree Swamp</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Conway Marina, Elm Street and Marina Drive</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">17 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Main Street and Pecan Grove Boulevard may begin to flood</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The US 501 Bypass may flood. Florence reached 21.16 feet.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which subdivisions flooded in Florence</h3><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Subdivision</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes where Florence's water reached</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sherwood</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">126</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">98</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Midland</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">49</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">33</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Pecan Grove</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">103</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">29</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Country Club Forest</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">57</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Lakeland</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">37</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">18</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By the county's map, Florence's water did not reach large parts of Conway. No home in Rosehaven, Oak Glenn, Woodland Lakes, Rivertown Row, Kingston Bay or Snowhill, or out US 501, is in either flood map.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="844" alt="Floodwater covering a street and the yards of single-story houses, with road signs standing in the water, in the Conway area after Hurricane Florence" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-USGov-Military-National_Guard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: SC National Guard. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: SC National Guard</a></span></div><figcaption>Floodwater on a street of houses in the Conway area after Florence.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How often it happens</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The river has reached major flood stage in 14 floods in the Weather Service's crest list. 6 of them came from 2015 through 2025.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Every flood on record that reached major flood stage at Conway"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Every flood on record that reached major flood stage at Conway</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Year</span><span role="columnheader">Highest river height</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2024</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.677" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.9 ft</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2021</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.709" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">15.6 ft</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2020</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.64" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.08 ft</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2018, Hurricane Florence</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.962" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21.16 ft</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2016, Hurricane Matthew</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.813" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17.89 ft</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2015</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.738" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">16.23 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1999, Hurricane Floyd</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.8" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17.6 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1998</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.673" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.8 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1996</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.655" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.4 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1983</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.659" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.5 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1945</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.709" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">15.6 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1928</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.809" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17.8 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1924</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.705" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">15.5 ft</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1908</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.664" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14.6 ft</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Highest height on the river gauge at the Conway Marina in each flood, newest first. Major flooding starts at 14 feet. The Weather Service's list has gaps in some years.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood insurance paid 109 claims in the city for 2018 losses; the middle claim was about $134,000. After Hurricane Matthew, the city used FEMA grants to buy 86 buildings, and after Hurricane Floyd in 1999 it bought 14. Land bought this way must stay open space.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you make an offer on any Conway house, we check both flood maps for it and read the seller's flood disclosure. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how to find out if a house flooded</a> shows every record we use.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood-insurance"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Do you need flood insurance in Conway, and what does it cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You must have it only if the house is in FEMA's high-risk zone and your loan is from a federally regulated lender. A lender can still ask for it anywhere.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the high-risk zone, a flood policy on a house usually costs about $560 a year in ZIP code 29526 and about $680 in 29527. Inside it, about $980 in either ZIP.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new federal flood policy takes effect 30 days after the application and payment are complete, unless it is bought when a home loan is made. So buy it with the house, not when a storm is coming. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> explains the other policies a house here can need.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Conway each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a $265,000 house you live in inside the city, the property tax is about $1,700 a year. A flood policy outside the high-risk zone adds about $560 to $680 if you want one.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year, $265,000 house</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Inside the city</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Just outside it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax, a home you live in</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $1,700</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $1,100, with the county's $89 stormwater fee</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Flood policy outside the high-risk zone, if you want one</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $560 to $680</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $560 to $680</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong>Total</strong></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong>About $2,300 to $2,400</strong></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><strong>About $1,600 to $1,700</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax as a second home or rental</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $4,300</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $3,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $654 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value. Just outside, it pays about $368, plus the stormwater fee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes a home you live in on 4 percent of its value, and a second home or rental on 6 percent. The owner must apply for the 4 percent rate. Inside the city, that makes a rental's bill about 2.5 times a home's. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> shows how to apply.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HOA fees depend on the subdivision, and many Conway streets have none. We get the fee for any house you like before you make an offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="home-prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Conway, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house or townhouse that resold inside the city in the past year usually went for about $265,000. Half sold for between about $220,000 and $340,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold about 120 new homes in the city in the same year, for about $295,000 in the middle. Condos are few: 14 of the 348 resales, at about $155,000.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home usually resold for in the past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home usually resold for in the past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, homes resold</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">36 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.559" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$235,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">17 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.613" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$255,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">327 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.632" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$265,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Socastee</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">296 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.694" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$290,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,004 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.73" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$305,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All of Horry County</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">8,569 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.777" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$325,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">418 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.95" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$395,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">961 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$420,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses and townhouses resold by their owners, not by a builder, and not condo units. Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Aynor had only 17 resales.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is not the cheapest town in the county. Homes in Loris and Aynor, two smaller inland towns, resold for less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count, about 670 houses were for sale with a Conway address, and 368 of them were new construction. 62 were on an acre or more. Our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">no-HOA homes guide</a> and <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places</a> include Conway.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting-out"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting out">What do homes rent for in Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD's fair market rent in the Conway ZIP codes, 29526 and 29527, is $1,630 a month for a three-bedroom. It is the rent plus utilities of an ordinary rental, a little under the middle of the market.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Bedrooms</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">HUD fair market rent, Conway ZIPs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,320</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Three</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,630</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In ZIP 29579, Carolina Forest, the three-bedroom figure is $2,230, about $600 more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the college, we have found August is the best month to find a new tenant, because new students arrive. Start marketing a month before the lease ends. Our <a href="/invest/student-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">student rental guide</a> covers renting near Coastal Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For any address, our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental analyzer</a> gives the rent and the costs. For nightly rentals, see <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what a nightly rental earns by town</a> and <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the short-term rental rules by town</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Conway?</h2><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Homes cost less than in the county as a whole, and new homes and land are for sale.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A downtown on the river, with Main Street and the Riverwalk.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A university inside the city, and the hospital about 10 minutes away.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>A few parts flood, and the river stays high for weeks. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check both flood maps for any house before you make an offer.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The city's property tax is higher than just outside it. <span class="c3-pc-do">We tell you which side of the city line a house is on, and its tax.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is about 25 minutes away without traffic; rush hour adds 5 to 10. <span class="c3-pc-do">We show you the drive from any house you like.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="conway-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Conway, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC a good place to live?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a buyer who wants a river town with a downtown and a university, about 25 minutes from the beach, at prices under the county's middle, yes. The trade is flooding in a few places near the river and the swamps.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Conway from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 25 minutes by car from downtown Conway to the beach in Myrtle Beach, without traffic, and about 25 minutes to Myrtle Beach International Airport.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Conway, SC flood?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a few places. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached; most of the rest are near the Waccamaw River, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $654 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value. Just outside the city, it pays about $368, plus an $89 stormwater fee.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 30,600 in 2025, by the Census Bureau's estimate, up from 24,849 at the 2020 Census.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. The FBI's Crime Data Explorer and SLED, South Carolina's state police agency, publish reported crime for each police agency.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which schools serve Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, and one of its attendance areas is named Conway. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census estimates</a>, <a href="https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/CNWS1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS river gauge</a>, <a href="https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02110704/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS gauge</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-claims-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood claims</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/smallarea/index.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4013" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4013</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-44/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-80/section-80.19" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44 CFR 80.19</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/residents_visitors/about_conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City history</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/71000785" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NRHP record</a>, <a href="https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/?id=218724" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCES</a>. Our counts from county parcels, flood maps and the past year's deeds. Listing counts in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives from downtown, without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waccamaw_River_Warehouse_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Conway City Hall, a brick building with a white portico of four columns and stairs up both sides, beside a white clock tower and palmetto trees. Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_city_hall_0782.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops.</div><div role="listitem">An older house under a live oak, a few blocks from Main Street. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_Residential_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener norefe