+
+			<p>Crested at 17.81 feet on October 13, 2016, the second highest in history behind Hurricane Floyd.&nbsp; Flooding along the nearby Black River was particularly severe, with water backing up across large portions of rural western Pender County.&nbsp; Multiple neighborhoods were evacuated along Canetuck Road between the Black and the Cape Fear Rivers.</p>
