+he University receives monthly allocations from the Horry County one-cent sales tax, totaling $17,047,068 in 
+fiscal year 2025. These funds are restricted for capital improvements and enable the University to invest in 
+infrastructure projects that benefit both the campus and the broader Horry County community. 
+C
+oastal Carolina University remains committed to managed growth and financial sustainability. Total enrollment 
+for Fall 2024 reached 11,348, marking a 14% increase over the past decade. Full-time equivalency (FTE) 
+enrollment for Fall 2024 was 10,997, representing a 17% increase from Fall 2014. Preliminary data for Fall 2025 
+indicates a potential record-setting enrollment. 
+Tu
+ition rates for the 2024–25 academic year remain unchanged for both in-state and out-of-state 
+undergraduate students. In-state tuition is set at $5,820 per semester, which is $259 (4.3%) below the average 
+rate for South Carolina’s four-year public institutions. Out-of-state tuition remains at $14,814 per semester. 
