+Part 1B 11.13 State FY22-23 
+Proviso
+ (CHE: Scholarship Awards)  A student 
+may receive a Palmetto Fellows or LIFE 
+scholarship award during the summer, in 
+addition to fall and spring semesters of an 
+academic year, provided continued 
+eligibility requirements are met as of the 
+end of the spring semester.  Students must 
+enroll full-time, which for purposes of the 
+summer award will require enrollment in at 
+least twelve hours over the course of the 
+summer.  The summer is defined as the 
+period between the end of the spring term 
+and prior to the opening of the fall term.  
+The total summer award per student may 
+not exceed half of the allowable academic 
+year award up to the cost of attendance and 
+must be reimbursed if less than twelve 
+hours for academic credit are not attempted 
+by the student during summer sessions.  If 
+awarded in the summer, a student’s total 
+award during his or her enrollment may not 
+exceed the amount that would otherwise be 
+provided under current semester limits 
+applied for the scholarship awards.  
